       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses that high raise the risk of significant hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated to 10 mg.\n- **A different drug or regimen**, if you want more blood pressure control than amlodipine 10 mg gives. Examples are adding an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
